Ryan,

I suspect the issue is that your application is running out of memory if its starting up and then crashing. By default, application instances are deployed using the 'small' instance type and limited to 256MB of memory. You should read the Configuring Shiny Applications <https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps/blob/master/guide/guide.md#configuring-shiny-applications> section in the Getting Started Guide, and try redeploying your application using a larger instance type. If it seems to still be crashing, we can look into it further and see what is going on here.

-Andy

