The issue here seems to be with the shinysky <https://github.com/analytixware/shinysky> package. ShinyApps is unable to build the package:

* installing to library '/usr/local/lib/R/site-library'

* installing *source* package 'shinysky' ...
** R
** inst
** preparing package for lazy loading
** help
*** installing help indices
** building package indices
** testing if installed package can be loaded
Warning in library(package, lib.loc = lib.loc, character.only = TRUE, logical.return = TRUE,  :
  there is no package called 'shiny'
Warning in library(package, lib.loc = lib.loc, character.only = TRUE, logical.return = TRUE,  :
  there is no package called 'RJSONIO'
Error : .onLoad failed in loadNamespace() for 'shinysky', details:
 call: fun(libname, pkgname)
error: could not find function "addResourcePath"
Error: loading failed
Execution halted
ERROR: loading failed
* removing '/usr/local/lib/R/site-library/shinysky'

I suspect this is because the shinysky package is missing a required dependency in it's DESCRIPTION <https://github.com/AnalytixWare/ShinySky/blob/master/DESCRIPTION> file (I think it should list 'shiny' in as an Import).

My recommendation would be to reach out to the package author, or send a pull request.

-Andy

